WHAT IS METAR?
  METAR (Meteorological Aerodrome Report) is the international standard format
  for reporting current weather at airports. It includes wind, visibility,
  temperature, pressure, sky conditions, and more. Example:

    KJFK 151856Z 28015KT 10SM BKN250 M01/M15 A3040 RMK AO2

  Decoded:
    KJFK      = JFK Airport, New York
    151856Z   = 15th day, 18:56 UTC
    28015KT   = Wind from 280° at 15 knots
    10SM      = Visibility 10 statute miles
    BKN250    = Broken clouds at 25,000 ft
    M01/M15   = Temperature -1°C, Dewpoint -15°C
    A3040     = Altimeter 30.40 inHg

